I        why: the host side of the link bounds what the card can move to and from host memory: streamed experts, the host pool and the all-reduce when it goes through host memory
I        fix: a slot with the card's full width and speed (the board manual says which slots share lanes), or no riser; nothing to do if the board has no faster slot
I   note power-cap-below-default: card 0000:03:00.0 (rank 0): the power cap is 250 W, below the card's default of 300 W
I        why: under a sustained load the power cap is what sets the clock on these cards (scripts/cardclock.py shows which limit binds)
I        fix: echo 300000000 | sudo tee /sys/class/drm/card0/device/hwmon/hwmon*/power1_cap restores the default, with the server stopped; nothing to do if the cap was lowered on purpose
I   note swap-in-use: 1.01 GiB of swap is in use
I        why: a host thread that faults on a swapped page stalls the step it is part of
I        fix: free memory, or turn swap off on a machine that only serves
I   note cpu-governor: the CPU governor is powersave with energy preference balance_performance
I        why: the host side of a step -- scheduling, sampling, the n-gram gather, launch bookkeeping -- is single-threaded per rank, and a core that ramps slowly shows as host gap between steps
I        fix: cpupower frequency-set -g performance, or echo performance | sudo tee /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/cpufreq/energy_performance_preference
